    <exercise number="315" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <list type="ordered">
          <item>ⓐ Explain why $$\left( {-\sqrt{n}} \right)^{2}$$ is always positive, for $$n \geq 0$$ .</item>
          <item>ⓑ Explain why $$- \left( \sqrt{n} \right)^{2}$$ is always negative, for $$n \geq 0$$ .</item>
        </list>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ when squaring a negative, it becomes a positive ⓑ since the negative is not included in the parenthesis, it is not squared, and remains negative</paragraph>
      </solution>
